Z||000005||Philphine||07-28-2000||11:13 AM||||not quite what you were asking but i think i have a way of getting a tall wing. and not a supra type. this one is more square and should look better on a fiero.<P>an f-40 wing for a mustang coupe /convertible. back when fieros first came out there was a guy who had an f-40 style wing. maybe they were available for fieros then but i've come to believe he got one made for a mustang. makes it look like a mini superbird. i'm hoping to get one for my '84 fiero coupe if that project gets off the ground.<P>the rear trunk/ decklid demensions are so close bettween a fiero coupe and non hatch back mustangs (late '80s-early '90s) that what ever wing fits on a mustang will fit and look good on a fiero. it gives you a lot more style options. plus some one (bam-bam?) recently mentioned that a newer mustang wing fits and looks good too. <P>the fiero wing is probaly one of the nicest stock wings around, but this lets you stand out a little (tastefully or tacky you'll have to judge). especially if you have more than one or are in an area where more people have them. <P>------------------<P><BR>'87 coupe (feral)<BR>'84 indy<p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 07-28-2000).]||||reg||1
